[E0427] Error: an `own` closure cannot hold a `str`
   ╭─[ err/166_str_kept_by_inference/main.wip:6:15 ]
   │
 6 │     own () => s.len()
   │               ┬  
   │               ╰── a `str` borrows bytes that live somewhere else
   │ 
   │ Help: `String` owns its bytes, and hands out a `str` with `toStr()`
   │ 
   │ Note: a `str`, a `&` reference, a `view struct` and what holds one borrow what lives somewhere else, so they stand in a parameter, a local, a result and a view's field, and not where they would outlive it
───╯
